# Swift / iOS Rules

## Project layout
- Each feature gets its own folder under `BriefIQ-iOS/Features/<Name>/`.
- A feature folder contains: `<Name>View.swift`, `<Name>ViewModel.swift`, plus colocated sub-views (`BriefingCard.swift`, `QueryRow.swift`, etc.).
- Shared utilities live in `BriefIQ-iOS/Core/` (Network, Models, Auth, Push).
- Tests live in `BriefIQ-iOS/Tests/`, one file per ViewModel.

## SwiftUI patterns
- Use the Observation framework (`@Observable`) on ViewModels — never `ObservableObject` / Combine.
- ViewModels expose `var` properties; views read them directly via `@State private var vm`.
- `async/await` everywhere. Never `DispatchQueue.main.async`.
- `URLSession` directly — no Alamofire. All networking goes through `Core/Network/APIClient.swift`.
- ViewModels call `APIClient`; views never touch `URLSession`.

## Persistence
- `SwiftData` is a local read-cache only.
- The backend is the source of truth — never persist user-authored data only locally.
- `Core/Auth/TokenStore.swift` uses Keychain for the JWT.

## Native APIs (preferred over third-party)
- `UserNotifications` for push.
- `ActivityKit` for Live Activities (monitoring status).
- `WidgetKit` for the Today widget.
- `App Intents` for Siri / Shortcuts.
- `AuthenticationServices` for Sign in with Apple.

## No third-party deps without explicit approval
- No SwiftLint, SnapKit, Alamofire, RxSwift, etc. unless asked.
- Apple frameworks first.

## Tests
- `XCTest` only. Add `@MainActor` to the test class for ViewModel tests.
- One test file per ViewModel, mirroring `Features/` layout.
- Mock `APIClient` via a static factory like `.mocked(returning:)`.
